@chapter 20 | International Organizations and Global Rankings

@intro
This chapter covers the **Bretton Woods institutions** (IMF, World Bank), the **WTO** and GATT (agreement on agriculture, subsidy boxes, TRIPS), the **G-20**, **World Economic Forum** and its indices, **ILO**, **ADB**, regional groups (**SAARC, BIMSTEC, ASEAN, BRICS, SCO, GCC, OPEC**), the global **reports** and who publishes them, and the size of the world's **largest economies**. It contains **{pyqs} PYQs and {ones} one-liners**.
@end

@section 20.1 | G-20 and Global Reports

@q 14:1-3

India held the **G-20 presidency** from **1 December 2022 to 30 November 2023**; the 18th summit was in **New Delhi** (9-10 September 2023) under the theme "**Vasudhaiva Kutumbakam: One Earth, One Family, One Future**". The logo shows the **earth on a lotus with seven petals**, for the seven continents; the **African Union** became a permanent member. Brazil's leader was **Lula da Silva**; Joko Widodo was Indonesia's president.

