@section 20.3 | IMF and World Bank

@q 14:15-17

@pyq U.P.P.C.S. (Pre) 2025
With reference to the International Monetary Fund and the World Bank, which of the following statements is/are not correct?
1. The World Bank and the IMF were established together and both are known as Bretton Woods institutions.
2. The heads of the IMF and the World Bank are traditionally from Italy and Germany respectively.
Select the correct answer from the code given below—
(a) Only 2
(b) Neither 1 nor 2
(c) Both 1 and 2
(d) Only 1
@ans (a)
@note The source prints **(d)**, but its own explanation shows statement 1 is **correct** and statement 2 **wrong**, so the incorrect statement is **only 2**, option (a). Both bodies came from the **Bretton Woods Conference (1944)**. By custom the **IMF** head is a **European** (now Kristalina Georgieva, Bulgaria) and the **World Bank** head an **American** (now Ajay Banga).
@end
@src 14:18

@q 14:19-22

@table
Body | Fact
**IMF** | Bretton Woods 1944; works from **1947**; HQ **Washington, D.C.**; lends for **temporary balance-of-payments deficits**; India a **founder member (27 December 1945)**
**SDR** | **"Paper gold"** (1969); value from 5 currencies (USD, euro, yuan, yen, pound)
**World Bank** (IBRD) | HQ **Washington, D.C.**; long-term **development loans**; **IDA** (1960) gives **soft loans** to the poorest
World Bank's NAIP (2006) | Four components
@end

