@q 14:35-36

@table
WTO fact | Detail
**GATT** | **General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade**, 1947-48; **Uruguay Round** (1986-94; **Arthur Dunkel** draft)
**WTO** | **1 January 1995**; HQ **Geneva**; **166 members** (Comoros and Timor-Leste joined 2024); DG **Ngozi Okonjo-Iweala** (after Roberto Azevedo, who followed Pascal Lamy)
Ministerial Conferences | 4th **Doha (Qatar), 2001**: Doha Development Agenda; 13th **Abu Dhabi**, 2024; 14th Yaoundé (Cameroon), 2026
Agreement on Agriculture | Three pillars: **market access, domestic support, export competition**
**Amber box** | Trade-distorting support (MSP, input subsidies); capped (**de minimis 10%** for developing countries)
**Blue box** | Payments tied to **production limits**
**Green box** | **Non-distorting** support (research, extension, income support)
**TRIPS** | Copyright, **trademarks**, **geographical indications**, **industrial designs**, patents, **integrated-circuit layouts**, trade secrets; not labour standards; plant varieties via **sui generis** law
National IPR Policy | **May 2016**; nodal body **DIPP** (now **DPIIT**)
@end

**Developing countries** also had to cut farm subsidies under the WTO, though less and over 10 years, so the Assertion in Q36 is false.

