**Ind-Aus ECTA** (in force **29 December 2022**) was India's first trade agreement with a developed country in over a decade. **MATES** (2023) lets young Indian graduates (18-30) work in Australia for up to two years.

@up UP link: **Varanasi** was the SCO's first Tourism and Cultural Capital (2022-23). UP hosted **G-20** meetings in **Lucknow, Agra, Varanasi and Greater Noida** during India's presidency, including the **Development Ministers' Meeting** at Varanasi (June 2023).

@trap
**G-20 Delhi 2023: lotus with 7 petals = 7 continents; African Union joined.** **WEO and GFSR = IMF; WDR = World Bank; HDR = UNDP; WIR = UNCTAD; Emissions Gap = UNEP; Gender Gap and TTCI = WEF; Wage and Social Protection reports = ILO.** **IMF and World Bank: Washington.** **India in IMF: 1945.** **SDR = paper gold.** **WTO 1995, Geneva; Doha = Qatar.** **Blue box = production-limited; green = non-distorting.** **TRIPS excludes labour standards.** **WEF: Klaus Schwab.** **ADB: Manila.** **BIMSTEC excludes Indonesia; GCC excludes Iran, Iraq.** **NDB first president K.V. Kamath.** **SCO full member 2017, Astana.**
@end

